<title>USA: General Re Q4 shr rises to $3.00.</title>
<headline>General Re Q4 shr rises to $3.00.</headline>
<dateline>STAMFORD, Conn 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr		 $3			 $2.75</p>
<p> Net		 248,100		  228,800</p>
<p> Oper revs	 2,220,800		2,029,600</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  81,872,803	     82,241,196</p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr		 $11			$9.92</p>
<p> Net		 893,500		  824,900</p>
<p> Oper revs	 8,192,100		7,146,200</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  80,251,342	     82,085,315</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: General Re Corp.</p>
<p>Net income for the quarter includes $0.17 per share of after-tax realized capital gains, compared to $0.23 shares of after-tax realized capital gains for the same period in 1995.</p>
<p>Consolidated net premiums written for the fourth quarter were $1.7 billion against $1.59 billion a year ago.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
</text>
